  "question": {
    "text": "A double star system consists of two stars $A$ and $B$ which have time period $T_A$ and $T_B$. Radius $R_A$ and $R_B$ and mass $M_A$ and $M_B$. Choose the correct option."
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\nIf $T_A>T_B$, then $R_A>R_B$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\nIf $T_A>T_B$, then $M_A>M_B$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\left(\\frac{T_A}{T_B}\\right)^2=\\left(\\frac{R_A}{R_B}\\right)^3$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$T_A=T_B$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "In case of binary star system angular velocity and hence the time period of both the stars are equal."
  }
